 with and create resources for learners of all ages, re aching over 151 million people globally. Through international partnerships, MediaWise works across 30 countries. With simple yet effective media and AI literacy skills, we aim to meet people where they are and walk with them through every step to determine what’s real and what’s not on the internet. Through MediaWise, everyone can do their part to reduce the spread of misinformation and elevate the facts. Explore our work Find our media and information literacy curriculum and resources Media Literacy Level up your AI understanding with curriculum and training AI Literacy See how we amplify media literacy through trusted voices Ambassador Program Learn about our youth-centered work Teen Creator Network Dive deeper into research and news coverage about our work See Mediawise in Action MediaWise works all over the world International Encuentre nuestros recursos de alfabetización mediática en español En Español Get started with online learning led by MediaWise experts Classes and Training MediaWise Team Alex Mahadevan MediaWise Director and Poynter Faculty Alex Mahadevan is faculty at Poynter and director of MediaWise, Poynter’s digital media literacy project that teaches people of all ages how to spot misinformation... Read More Brittani Kollar Deputy Director, MediaWise Brittani Kollar is the deputy director of MediaWise, Poynter’s digital media literacy project. In this role, she oversees MediaWise’s global strategic partnerships, programming and operations,... Read More Sean Marcus Interactive Learning Designer, MediaWise As the Interactive Learning Designer for MediaWise, Sean Marcus designs and develops learning material for a wide range of audiences and purposes, ranging from senior... Read More Jessi Hollis McCarthy Program Specialist, MediaWise Jessi Hollis McCarthy is the program specialist of MediaWise, Poynter’s digital media literacy project that teaches people of all ages how to spot misinformation o